Sixteen (16) boxers, the most in any weight division at the 1932 Olympic Games, competed in the welterweight division. " [:a {:href "/athletes/2925"} "Bruno Ahlberg"] " of Finland impressed in the early rounds, earning a standing ovation from the crowd for the performance against the Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/4109"} "Luciano Fabbroni"] ". In contrast, the USA’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/8667"} "Eddie Flynn"] " had a difficult time in his quarter-final. He had knocked " [:a {:href "/athletes/7957"} "Dick Barton"] " to the canvas early in the fight, but the South African recovered and had a barnstorming final round. Flynn’s early advantage proved just enough to see him through."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Another quarter-final saw the defeat of one of the title favorites, the Mexican " [:a {:href "/athletes/4594"} "Al Romero"] ". Romero had " [:a {:href "/athletes/3447"} "Dave McCleave"] " of Britain on the canvas on no less than five occasions, but the last one was the result of a low blow and, having already been given a warning, he was disqualified. His protests came to nothing. No less than an hour later, he had signed a professional contract and made his début in the same ring six weeks later."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The semi-final round saw Flynn box his way past McCleave, while Ahlberg went down to defeat against " [:a {:href "/athletes/3597"} "Erich Campe"] ", a German policeman. The final was a close one, but Flynn was awarded the decision by 60-59 to the delight of the American crowd."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Eddie Flynn, originally from New Orleans, was a dentistry student at Loyola University who supplemented his income by working as a janitor for $60 a month. He was reputed to have been undefeated in 144 bouts in the amateur code.  Picked out by " [:em {} "Time Magazine"] " as the outstanding fighter at the 1932 AAU finals, he insisted he had no intention of turning professional, but four months after his Olympic triumph, he turned professional. He lost seven of his 30 pro bouts and never fought for a title, although the money earned helped him set up a dental practice."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/8667"} "Eddie Flynn"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/3597"} "Erich Campe"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2925"} "Bruno Ahlberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/3447"} "Dave McCleave"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/1716"} "Carl Jensen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/4109"} "Luciano Fabbroni"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style